From 25e409b82d53f57a1c5caf3d7b104c9549156507 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Graeme Smecher <gsmecher@t0.technology>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:04:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] target/microblaze: migrate the CPU's registers

vmstate_mb_cpu is version 0, but its env field (all of the CPU's
registers: r0-r31, pc, msr, esr, ...) is tagged version 1. Fields newer
than their description are skipped, so the registers were never saved or
loaded: a restored MicroBlaze came back with its power-on registers (pc
at the reset vector) and only cpu_common's halted and interrupt_request.

Make the description version 1, matching the field. Streams from before
this change carry no registers, so they can't be restored anyway: the
minimum version is 1 too, so that loading one fails rather than restoring
a CPU without its state.

Fixes: 77f63e1dadb3 ("target/microblaze: Fill in VMStateDescription for cpu")
---
 target/microblaze/machine.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/microblaze/machine.c b/target/microblaze/machine.c
index d24def39..4e5ac1ec 100644
--- a/target/microblaze/machine.c
+++ b/target/microblaze/machine.c
@@ -100,7 +100,7 @@ static VMStateField vmstate_cpu_fields[] = {
 
 const VMStateDescription vmstate_mb_cpu = {
     .name = "cpu",
-    .version_id = 0,
-    .minimum_version_id = 0,
+    .version_id = 1,
+    .minimum_version_id = 1,
     .fields = vmstate_cpu_fields,
 };
